---This API allows you to create a conformance pack template with an Amazon Web Services Systems Manager document (SSM document). To deploy a conformance pack using an SSM document, first create an SSM document with conformance pack content, and then provide the DocumentName in the PutConformancePack API. You can also provide the DocumentVersion.
---@class aws.config_service.TemplateSSMDocumentDetails
---@field DocumentName aws.config_service.SSMDocumentName The name or Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the SSM document to use to create a conformance pack. If you use the document name, Config checks only your account and Amazon Web Services Region for the SSM document.
---@field DocumentVersion? aws.config_service.SSMDocumentVersion The version of the SSM document to use to create a conformance pack. By default, Config uses the latest version.

